  <running_head>De Duellis.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>QuÆsT.</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">buisset. Et quia ex condicto</l>
    <l n="2">cum adversario congreditur,</l>
    <l n="3">sedatâ mente, &amp; quidem ex</l>
    <l n="4">intervallo, non in continenti,</l>
    <l n="5">ut vim vi non repellat; adeo-</l>
    <l n="6">que in nullo moderamen in-</l>
    <l n="7">culpatæ tutelæ servaverit; per</l>
    <l n="8">allegata in seq. Idem quod di-</l>
    <l n="9">cendum de adversario,qui do-</l>
    <l n="10">mum ivit, gladium petiturus.</l>
    <l n="11">Injustam enim habuit depu-</l>
    <l n="12">gnandi causam,quin non necef-</l>
    <l n="13">sariam. Incurrit in periculum,</l>
    <l n="14">quod domi manendo evitare</l>
    <l n="15">poterat. Unde nec in conscien-</l>
    <l n="16">tiâ redire tenebatur, licet se</l>
    <l n="17">reversurum promisisset. Quod</l>
    <l n="18">in malis fidem rescindere non</l>
    <l n="19">sit peccatum; hoc quippe nihil</l>
    <l n="20">aliud est, quam vinculum ini-</l>
    <l n="21">quitatis dissolvere. Ne ad-</l>
    <l n="22">dam, quod uterque vindictæ</l>
    <l n="23">cupiditate stimulatus, propter</l>
    <l n="24">illatas vel acceptas injurias su-</l>
    <l n="25">scipiat duelli conditionem: ut</l>
    <l n="26">neuter sit extra legis pœnam</l>
    <l n="27">constitutus.</l>
  </main_text>
